  "notes": "A ground-floor clinic in a beige-brick apartment block, drawn as a cutaway at its ceiling so the interior - which is the project - reads from above: the apartments above are left off. From the street views (granite piers, a dark steel frame, vertical oak slat panels alternating with tall frosted windows, the entrance, the sign fascia) and the interior views (warm plaster partitions that end in curves, a big curved wall at the entrance sweeping round to the reception, the reception's concrete counter against an oak wall with shelves and the concrete sign panel, rust-red sofas with round oak tables, a corridor with rounded ends, white treatment rooms with their chairs and cabinets). No plan is published: the room layout, the number of treatment rooms (four), the bay rhythm of the front and the depth are estimates; the street is taken as south. Refined 24 Sep 2026 against the street view: the tall frosted windows now read as pale panes in dark steel frames (they were dark glass), the shopfront sits in a grey granite frame (piers and fascia) with the dark sign over the door, the floor is the pale porcelain of the interiors, the treatment rooms have their dark-framed frosted windows to the back, and the waiting area has its cluster of disc pendants; one street tree, as photographed."
